+# Regional client portal integration
+
+## Context
+The Kanook frontend needs the existing account and QC boundary, persistent
+project configuration, key management, support grievances and project run history.
+
+## What we did
+Prepared migration 16 for project settings, key labels, private grievances and
+project/job associations. Added validated routes using existing membership and
+permission checks. Added an explicit portal-origin allowlist and corresponding
+Terraform/storage CORS configuration. These changes are local and undeployed.
+
+## How
+Reused account sessions and CSRF, project-scoped keys, transactional QC submission,
+and regional storage. Stable idempotency keys deduplicate grievance and job
+retries. Exact portal origins extend only the browser account boundary; operator
+authentication is unchanged. Migration 15 is not rewritten.
+
+## Why
+A separate authentication service and shared browser API key would duplicate or
+weaken the deployed boundary. Reusing QC submission preserves enrollment,
+execution and pricing behavior. Raw uploads are not implicitly QC datasets.
+
+## Architecture
+Browser -> regional account/CSRF -> authorized project routes -> regional store.
+Project dispatch -> existing QC submission -> existing workers. File bytes go
+directly to GCS using the existing resumable intake contract.
+
+## Open questions
+The portal's ten in-process integration tests pass using disposable local stores;
+the deployment/PostgreSQL gates have not been run. Release requires the real
+GCP target, schema migration, exact portal origin, bucket/SMTP configuration and
+worker enrollment. Grievances persist but need an operator triage surface.
+Automatic intake-to-manifest translation remains a separate API requirement.
